+# Claire Trading — technical-debt, efficiency and UI review (2026-11-11)
+
+Read-only review at commit `61229a2`. No project file, service or database
+row was changed. Four parallel reviewers read every file in `app/`, `web/`,
+`bin/`, `mcp/` and `systemd/` in full; I ran the tests and linter, walked
+every dashboard page at desktop and phone width, timed the endpoints, and
+re-checked the findings marked **[V]** against the code or the live
+database myself. Unmarked items are a reviewer's reading of the code that I
+did not re-check. The 2026-11-03 review covered security; this one does not
+repeat it.
+
+**Summary.** The safety design is sound and the 2026-11-03 fixes held, but
+the code has grown by re-implementing things per feature instead of sharing
+them, and that duplication has started to produce wrong numbers on screen
+and a few real bugs on the money path. Nothing is slow today; the
+efficiency problems are wasted LLM turns and oversized polled payloads, not
+response times. The UI's biggest gaps are that no page answers "what do I
+hold, what protects it, what is pending", totals mix SGD and USD, and paper
+versus live is easy to miss.
+
+One thing to know about this review itself: `tests/test_smoke.py` runs
+against the live services when they are up, so each of my three full test
+runs sent one real "status?" chat turn to Claire and one live quote request.
+
+---
+
+## Status
+
+Updated at the end of the work on 2026-11-11. The sections below are the
+review as written and describe the code BEFORE these changes (line numbers
+have moved; `app/dashboards.py` is now a 330-line shell over `app/dash/`).
+
+**Done and live**
+
+- **Bugs:** B1–B7, B9–B15 and the five "smaller ones". B6 in full: the
+  ledger check runs every custodian pass, and `_position_drift` compares
+  the book's holdings with what Saxo holds (flagged after two passes;
+  disarms live trading on a live account). B8: a chat thread is now a
+  resumed session, not a flattened transcript — input tokens per turn fell
+  from about 50,000 to 4,000–6,500 in a live two-turn check, with no
+  refusal. All 35 past refusals cited `[reasoning_extraction]`; the rate
+  on real use still has to be watched.
+- **Logging (§3.5):** timestamps, thread deaths, throttled lines for
+  swallowed failures, tracebacks for jobs, duties and HTTP 500s, and
+  credentials scrubbed from every line. Slow scheduled jobs run off the
+  tick; the custodian, price triggers and reconcile stay inline.
+- **§3.1 shared code:** `app/exchanges.py` (+ `DESK` in `nav.js`),
+  `app/states.py`, `app/accounting/holdings.py`, `app/origin.py`,
+  `app/dash/claire_api.py`.
+- **§3.2:** the request handler is out of the closure — `app/dash/`
+  `handler.py`, `views_system.py`, `views_runs.py`, `views_orders.py`,
+  `actions.py`, `common.py`, `ctx.py`, `usage.py`.
+- **§3.3:** `db.tx` / `repo.tx`; state changes, approval authorisation,
+  `cancel_failed` and order edits are each one transaction.
+- **§3.4:** `PRAGMA user_version`; three side tables defined in
+  `schema.sql`; ten indexes.
+- **§3.6:** every setting documented in `etc/claire.env.example`;
+  `bin/claire watchdog` and a timer template for crash recovery (not
+  installed); a clear error for the optional `langchain-openai`.
+- **§4:** SDK timeout and concurrency cap; `fetch_page` returns the
+  article; Twelve Data budget in credits, halved per process; gzip and
+  ETag revalidation; health rows written on change only.
+- **§5:** dead scripts, units, CLIs, functions and page code removed.
+- **§6 UI** (item numbers from section 6): the "Today" home view (1); the
+  PAPER / LIVE ARMED indicator and approvals badge (2); per-currency money
+  (3); a shorter path — "Buy…" / "Sell…" forms land on their approval card
+  (4, in part); in-page confirmations everywhere (5); Reject asks first
+  (6); "plan only" as a warning (7, in part); the grouped menu (8); phone
+  viewport and standards mode (9); working deep links (10); the Runs page
+  search and status filter (11); link colour and dark colour-scheme (12);
+  one vocabulary in page text, raw ids in tooltips (13); times with their
+  zone and countdowns (14); a shared "updated / paused / cannot reach"
+  pill (15); edits and open sections survive a refresh (16); the approval
+  card in plain words with linked sources (17); labels, keyboard access and
+  contrast (18); chat history on reload, no double-send, tool calls in
+  words (19). The Saxo page opens on SIM; a live account is marked.
+- **Saxo account page:** an unpriced position no longer counts as a loss,
+  and a quote for a different company of the same ticker is not used.
+- **Tests:** 745 → about 960; the suite 95 s → 48 s; the live smoke test
+  is opt-in; `tests/preview_server.py` shows the pages on made-up data
+  with nothing real reachable.
+
+**Not done, and why**
+
+- **NSE 2027 holidays:** only the fixed dates until NSE publishes its
+  circular (December). The maintainer warns from 15 December.
+- **One `SaxoClient`** (§3.1): five request wrappers remain. Unifying the
+  broker's HTTP layer cannot be verified without placing orders.
+- **Editable stop-loss / take-profit** (§6 item 7): needs new order-amend
+  calls at Saxo, which were not built or tested unattended. "Plan only"
+  is now a warning badge.
+- **`market.price_in`** (§3.1): each of the eleven sites already holds a
+  quote and wants only the rate, with its own failure policy; a helper
+  would have fitted one of them.
+- **Positions:** the watcher's per-side grouping, `repo.position` and the
+  chat tool's cost breakdown keep their own queries.
+- **§3.2:** the GET/POST dispatch is still an if-chain, and about 300
+  lines of logic are still inline in `do_POST`.
+- **§4:** the custodian still asks Saxo once per working order; `/api/runs`
+  and `/api/approvals` are compressed but not slimmed; HTTP/1.0 (a
+  connection per request); N+1 queries on Portfolio and Trades;
+  analyst research and extraction as one session is built but OFF
+  (`CLAIRE_SDK_ANALYST_ONE_SESSION=1`), unproven on real runs.
+- **§3.6:** floats in `check_risk`'s percentage test; the shared
+  `SaxoBroker` has no lock around its throttle.
+- **Kept on purpose:** `mcp/` and the `mcp_servers` table, the four
+  non-Claude providers, `repo.apply_split`, the old backups under `var/`.
+
+**Seen in real logs**
+
+- Twelve Data answered 429 on most FX and quote calls in the first hour
+  (the budget counted calls, not credits, across two processes). Fixed;
+  worth a look at `var/log/*.log` after a day.
+
