+---
+
+## 2. Fix first — bugs found along the way
+
+These are not debt; they are wrong behaviour today. Ordered by risk to
+money or to the quality of Claire's decisions.
+
+> **Update, 2026-11-11 (same day):** B1, B2, B3 and B6 are fixed in the
+> working tree, with tests in `tests/test_money_path_review_1111.py`.
+> B6 is fixed in part: the ledger's own consistency check now runs on
+> every custodian run, but a book-vs-venue *position* comparison still
+> does not exist (`Custodian._drift` says why). The rows below describe
+> the behaviour before the fix; line numbers have moved.
+>
+> B4 is fixed too (`tests/test_search.py`). The cause was not a broken
+> parser: DuckDuckGo answers the desk with its bot check (HTTP 202). The
+> keyless path now reads the Bing News and Google News RSS feeds — news
+> headlines only, not a general web search — and an outage raises instead
+> of returning an empty list. The screener now sees a `TAVILY_API_KEY`.
+>
+> B9 is fixed (`tests/test_agent_prompts.py`). Each kind of role has its
+> own prompt template, every stored prompt passes through
+> `registry.render_prompt`, and `seeds.seed` upgrades a prompt that is
+> still word-for-word the first template to version 2 (the old text stays
+> in `agent_versions`). B8 has not been re-measured yet.
+>
+> §3.5 (logging) is done in part (`app/logsetup.py`, `tests/test_logging.py`):
+> both services log with timestamps, uncaught thread deaths are logged,
+> the silent handlers leave a throttled line, and scheduler jobs, custodian
+> duties and dashboard 500s leave a traceback. Not done: the per-source
+> failure counter for the maintainer, and moving scheduler jobs off the
+> tick (a slow job is now logged, but still blocks the others).
+>
+> B5, B7, B12 and B13 are fixed (`tests/test_display_review_1111.py`).
+> Totals are one figure per account currency (`portfolio.totals_by_currency`,
+> `perCcy` in `nav.js`) and position weights are within one currency;
+> `/api/feed` returns the latest events and the Trading page polls with
+> `since`; Markets and Watchlist share `deskExchange` in `nav.js`, which
+> never guesses; no page redefines a shared-script function any more
+> (`orders.html` did too, with `ago`). Open: the Saxo page's "Unrealised
+> P/L" looked out of scale against the account total when viewed — not
