+| # | What | Where | |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| B1 | **A failed sell-review launch still counts as a fired alert.** When a trailing alert breaches and claire-api is down, slow (10 s timeout) or returns an error, `start_sell_review` swallows the failure and returns `None`; the watcher then records the fire anyway. No review is created, nothing is logged, one of the day's fires is used up and the next alert needs a further 3% fall. | `app/dashboards.py:3425-3436`, `app/watcher.py:268-273` | [V] |
+| B2 | **An order cancelled at its time limit can lose a fill.** After a successful venue cancel the custodian marks the order `expired` without a final status check. A fill that landed between this tick's poll and the cancel is never booked, because expired orders are not polled again. The window is seconds and only matters on Saxo. `_settle_ended` does it properly but only runs when the cancel raises. | `app/custodian.py:337-358` | [V] |
+| B3 | **Stale FX rates are booked silently.** `Market._cached` returns the last good value on a fetch failure with no age limit, and a scalar rate cannot carry the `stale` flag. That rate goes into the immutable `executions.fx_rate`, order sizing and the watcher. The 2026-11-03 fix (a failed lookup raises) only holds until a rate has been cached once. | `app/tools/market.py:121-130, 225-242, 467-493` | |
+| B4 | **Web search returns nothing, on every run.** `TAVILY_API_KEY` is empty, so `web_search` falls back to scraping DuckDuckGo, which returns no results. A reviewer counted 165 of 167 calls empty across the last 38 runs; the transcript I sampled shows three empty searches, then guessed URLs returning 403s. The news agent is working from one Yahoo page of navigation text. Separately, the screener would not use a key even if set: `screener_pick` is called without `env` and `catalyst_notes` defaults it to `{}`. | `app/tools/search.py:26-50`, `app/api/server.py:143`, `app/screener.py:137-138` | [V] |
+| B5 | **Portfolio, Mission Control and Trades totals add SGD and USD.** `total_value` sums `value_base` across accounts with different base currencies; "paper cash", "market value", "equity", realized P/L and fees are all shown as one unlabelled number. | `app/portfolio.py:223-250`, `web/index.html:732-739`, `web/portfolio.html:153-164`, `web/trades.html:75-80` | [V] |
+| B6 | **The daily "drift check" checks nothing.** `_drift` compares the book to `broker_snapshots.cash`, but `snapshot_brokers` always writes `cash=None` (21 of 21 rows) and no adapter returns a `positions` key. `repo.assert_invariants` says "the custodian calls it on a timer"; nothing in production calls it. | `app/custodian.py:612-639, 698-701`, `app/accounting/repo.py:571-590` | [V] |
+| B7 | **The Trading page's activity feed is frozen.** The page calls `/api/feed` with no `since`, and the server returns the oldest 300 events. It currently shows ids 1–300 (August to 5 November) while events run to 589, and re-downloads the same 70 KB every 8 seconds. | `web/trading.html:347`, `app/dashboards.py:952-955` | [V] |
+| B8 | **A third of Claire-chat calls are refused.** 35 of 122 `claire_chat` calls failed with "safeguards flagged this message". Each turn flattens the whole history into one user prompt ("Conversation so far: Richard: … You: …"), which is the likely trigger (not proven), and each retry is a full subprocess with 20–30k input tokens. | `app/providers/claude_sdk.py:171-201`, `app/graph/claire_agent.py:232-284` | [V] count |
+| B9 | **Every agent's stored system prompt contains a literal `{ticker}`.** Only the analyst path substitutes it. Bull, bear, arbiter, recorder, screener and chat are told they are "analysing {ticker}" and to "use your tools", though four of them have none. | `app/providers/seeds.py:28-33, 100-113` | [V] |
+| B10 | **Hong Kong tickers have no canonical form, so charts fail.** Scans emit unpadded codes (`HKEX:861`), `yahoo_symbol()` never pads, and agents improvise `0861.HK`, `00861.HK`. Padding logic exists in seven places with three conventions. A reviewer found "no chart" errors in 44 of 125 run folders. | `app/tools/market.py:89-93`, `app/tools/tradingview.py:199-204, 400-401` | |
